    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc. is a public company traded under the ticker LUMN and headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana. According to its website, it operates a global fiber network and provides secure networking, edge cloud and AI-ready infrastructure intended to connect people, data and applications. It describes itself as the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy, saying its fiber footprint reaches across markets and reduces latency where it matters.\n\nThe company says its network is built to support AI workloads across high-bandwidth and multicloud connections, with programmable, consumption-based service, diverse 100G paths and automatic failover. Its site cites customer work with the New York Yankees, American Family Care, Arctic Glacier and Prometheus Hyperscale, which the company says anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady. It also states that its network provides security for retail transactions and protection from DDoS attacks.\n\nCorporate records identify the company by CIK 0000018926. Its recorded law exposure is concentrated in Louisiana, with a count of 57, and no lawsuits are listed.",
